<title>GERMANY: Bonn buys 15 training helicopters from Eurocopter.</title>
<headline>Bonn buys 15 training helicopters from Eurocopter.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franco-German venture Eurocopter said on Thursday it had won an order for 15 training helicopters from Germany's defence procurement office worth around 95 million marks.</p>
<p>Seven EC 135 helicopters, built at the Eurocopter's Donauwoerth plant, will be delivered in 1998 and the rest in the following year, the company said.</p>
<p>Eurocopter is a joint venture between Daimler-Benz Aerospace AG, a unit of Daimler-Benz AG, and France's state-owned Aerospatiale.</p>
